        "input": {
          "level": "preferred",
          "summary": "Add mutual carve-outs (confidentiality/data, indemnities, gross negligence, wilful misconduct, fraud, IP infringement) outside the liability caps",
          "comment": "[Playbook] The caps in Sections 9.1/9.2 are mutual and 12-month based, which works for us, but they currently swallow confidentiality, data protection and security breaches (Section 9.1(c)(2) even excludes data loss entirely) as well as gross negligence, wilful misconduct, fraud and IP infringement. We have added a single mutual carve-out provision so that those items and the Section 8 indemnities sit outside the cap, consistent with our standard position; we are happy to keep the caps themselves as drafted.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "insert_after",
              "paragraphId": "p0121",
              "numbering": "9.3",
              "text": "9.3 Exclusions from Limitations. Notwithstanding Sections 9.1, 9.2 and 10 (including Subsection 9.1(c)(2)), neither party's liability is limited or excluded in respect of: (a) a party's breach of its confidentiality, data protection or security obligations (including under the AECI); (b) a party's indemnification obligations under Section 8; (c) a party's gross negligence, wilful misconduct or fraud; and (d) a party's infringement of the other party's intellectual property rights."
            }
          ]
